                  <msItem>
                     <title>Kalendarium, etc.</title>
                     <note type="MLGB3_generalNotes">A letter in the front of BL, Add. 6156 connects
                        Add. 6156--62 with Christ Church Canterbury on the strength of the obvious
                        provenance of this manuscript and Add. 6159, and the possible descent of the
                        MSS. from the 16th century in the manor of Charlwood (Surrey), which
                        belonged to Christ Church Cathedral Canterbury; but Add. 6156 is an Italian
                        manuscript from S. Maria in Trastevere, Rome.</note>
                     <msItem>
                        <title>Kalendarium, formulary, surveys, etc.</title>
                     </msItem>
